&nbsp;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88edc14"}, {"id": "77ac37", "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88edc15"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88edc16", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edb"], "question": {"text": "A wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> connected across the right gap of a meter bridge. When a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is connected on the left gap by using a resistance box, the balance length is found to be at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the left end. If the resistivity of the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, then value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "8e0e31", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>63</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88edc17"}, {"id": "63f980", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef0c677dc36a88edc18"}, {"id": "f24fae", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>66</mn></