orrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc73"}, {"id": "8ee1ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc74"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc75", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "A square-shaped wire with a resistance of each side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is bent to form a complete circle. The resistance between two diametrically opposite points of the circle in a unit of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> will is,&nbsp; _____."}, "options": [{"id": "6200e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc76"}, {"id": "e4e44b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc77"}, {"id": "dbe358", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc78"}, {"id": "62c80f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc79"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<p>Four resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;&nbsp;make the arms of a quadrilateral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>. Across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is a battery of emf&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi></math> and internal resistance negligible. The potential difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>D</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is __________</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2a1c96a4-3846-4257-9749-5b7714a8b313-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 197px; height: 175px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "519dc5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7b"}, {"id": "a67136", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7c"}, {"id": "f3aeac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7d"}, {"id": "abb9de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc7f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> AC source is connected to a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> lamp and an additional resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> in series (as shown in figure) to run the lamp at its peak brightness, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> (in ohm) will be</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Facd362ed-e47c-4eac-bef5-9fa0c13afa20-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 182px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "faded1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc80"}, {"id": "9cd518", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc81"}, {"id": "3e47df", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc82"}, {"id": "520bf3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc83"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc84", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b9"], "question": {"text": "To determine the resistance $(R)$ of a wire, a circuit is designed below. The $V-I$ characteristic curve for this circuit is plotted for the voltmeter and the ammeter readings as shown in figure. The value of $R$ is ______ $\\Omega$.\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FK4bbpJ2wVDkmLLMaNHkodo_mttVD857_MbrIQUSt6xg.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "3d0487", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc85"}, {"id": "c7982a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc86"}, {"id": "921820", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc87"}, {"id": "ce8f13", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc88"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:01.063Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:01.063Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4ef1c677dc36a88edc8f"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T